from assessment import add, save

add('0001',1971,'year','The modern P versus NP problem dates to Cook’s 1971 work and Levin’s independent work, published in 1973. Earlier questions about efficient proof search are historical precursors.',('cook','clay'))
add('6530',1970,'circa','Estimated origin in the formative 1960s–1970s study of polynomial time and space. Savitch’s 1970 theorem clarified polynomial space; the quantified-formula presentation and later IP characterization are subsequent formulations.',('book','alternation'))
add('6531',1970,'circa','Estimated origin in early time-versus-space complexity. Logarithmic-space classes were studied in the 1960s; the circuit-value characterization became standard with P-completeness in the 1970s. No unique first posing is identified.',('parallel','book'))
add('0015',1960,'range','The explicit unrestricted circuit-lower-bound challenge grew out of circuit complexity in the 1960s–1970s. This dates the underlying problem family; the precise polynomial-time, length-preserving multi-output formulation is a later normalization.',('book',),end_year=1975)
add('0004',1970,'year','Savitch’s 1970 work on deterministic versus nondeterministic space is the standard historical anchor. The directed-reachability formulation expresses the same logspace question.',('savitch',))
add('0002',1971,'circa','Estimated origin with the development of NP and its complement in the early 1970s. Cook–Reckhow’s 1979 paper gives the later proof-system characterization used by this card.',('cookreckhow','book'))
add('0021',1971,'range','The nonuniform strengthening of P versus NP emerged in the 1970s and was a central hypothesis by the 1980 Karp–Lipton work. The interval is a historical estimate, not an identified first statement.',('book','natural'),end_year=1980)
add('6532',1976,'year','Stockmeyer’s 1976 paper introduced and studied the polynomial-time hierarchy. Strictness of its successive levels is a foundational question of that framework.',('foundation',))
add('0020',1980,'circa','Estimated origin in the late-1970s/early-1980s study of nonuniform complexity and circuit upper bounds for exponential time. The cited modern survey records the longstanding problem; no unique first posing is established.',('primary',))
add('0016',1971,'range','An exponential nonuniform strengthening of the SAT lower-bound question from early complexity theory. The decade is approximate; the card’s exact clause-incidence encoding is a later specification and is not identified with uniform ETH.',('book','sparse'),end_year=1980)
add('6535',1986,'range','Estimated origin in the late-1980s development of bounded-depth threshold circuits and their comparison with logarithmic-depth circuits. Later uniform arithmetic results do not date the original nonuniform separation question.',('boot','division'),end_year=1990)
add('7161',2011,'by','This specific NEXP-versus-threshold-circuits frontier was already present around the 2011 ACC lower-bound breakthrough. Threshold-circuit lower-bound questions themselves are older; 2011 is a conservative anchor for this stronger-class formulation.',('primary','williams-pdf'))
add('0017',2018,'by','The constant-loss formula-size version is recorded in the 2018 survey. Its KRW ancestor is the 1995 depth-composition question; the cited 2023 paper distinguishes these formulations, so the original date is not silently assigned to the stronger formula variant.',('primary','original','projections'))
add('1056',1987,'circa','Estimated origin at the 1987 Razborov–Smolensky lower bounds for prime-modulus circuits, which left the composite-modulus ACC frontier. This dates the surviving majority-versus-ACC problem rather than the 2012 textbook.',('primary','symmetric-2026'))
add('6534',1977,'year','Berman and Hartmanis proposed the polynomial-time isomorphism conjecture in their 1977 paper.',('original',))
add('6817',1970,'circa','The question combines the separate small-space and polynomial-time approaches to reachability that were available around Savitch’s 1970 theorem. The simultaneous guarantee is the longstanding obstacle; this is an approximate historical date.',('primary','sublinear'))
add('7158',1976,'circa','Estimated from the establishment of the polynomial hierarchy and its relationship to polynomial space in the 1970s. This is the PH-versus-PSPACE comparison, not the stronger claim that every hierarchy level is distinct.',('primary',),sources=[{'title':'The Polynomial-Time Hierarchy — Stockmeyer (1976)','url':'https://research.ibm.com/publications/the-polynomial-time-hierarchy'}])
add('0018',1971,'circa','Estimated origin in early NP/coNP theory and the search for problems with short certificates on both sides but no efficient algorithm. Older “good characterization” ideas are precursors; no single first statement of this exact class comparison is identified.',('primary',))
add('6533',1997,'year','Reinhardt and Allender’s paper appeared at FOCS 1997 and in journal form in 2000. Later work explicitly attributes the NL-versus-UL question to that paper; unambiguous computation itself is older.',('nonuniform',),sources=[{'title':'On the Power of Unambiguity in Logspace — Pavan, Tewari and Vinodchandran (2012)','url':'https://cse.unl.edu/~vinod/papers/ptv_cc12.pdf','locator':'Introduction, p. 644, historical attribution'}])
add('0019',1970,'range','Estimated origin in the 1970s circuit-versus-formula and parallel-complexity program. The linear-size-circuit restriction is a particular normalization of the longstanding question about the power of sharing intermediate results.',('primary','balancing'),end_year=1980)
add('6168',2015,'year','The specific implication from unrestricted many-one NP-hardness of MCSP to EXP circuit lower bounds is posed in the 2015 work, with a 2017 journal version. MCSP itself is much older.',('primary','journal'))
add('7243',2007,'year','Regan’s July 2007 problem entry asks for linear-size circuits for this exact stable ternary compaction task.',('question',))
add('4786',1973,'by','The NP-hardness question was already considered by Levin before his 1973 NP-completeness publication, according to the historical account in the cited paper. Circuit minimization as a task predates NP-completeness.',('assumptions',))
add('6977',2009,'by','The explicit unrestricted quasilinear-time SAT lower-bound target is recorded in Fortnow’s 2009 survey and the 2016 lower-bound column. SAT lower bounds and time–space tradeoffs are older; the sources here do not identify the first posing of this exact target.',('primary','column'))
add('4988',1991,'circa','Estimated from the introduction of TFNP by Megiddo and Papadimitriou in 1991. The existence of a complete problem for this semantic total-search class is a longstanding structural question; the exact first posing is not pinned down.',('definitions','primary'),sources=[{'title':'On total functions, existence theorems and computational complexity (1991)','url':'https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3975(91)90200-L'}])
add('7524',1970,'circa','Estimated origin with exponential-time complexity classes in the 1970s. Asser’s 1955 spectrum-complement question is an older related problem about NE versus coNE; it is not the same as this NEXP-versus-coNEXP card.',('classes','spectra','thapen'))
add('1054',1990,'circa','Estimated origin in the late-1980s/early-1990s threshold-circuit lower-bound program. The card’s exponential lower bound for an NP-explicit family is a specific strong target; no unique first posing is identified.',('primary','chen-2018'))
add('0293',1970,'year','This asks to improve the quadratic deterministic-space simulation from Savitch’s 1970 theorem. The modern tree-evaluation and catalytic formulations are later connections to that old space-simulation question.',('primary',),sources=[{'title':'Relationships between nondeterministic and deterministic tape complexities — Savitch (1970)','url':'https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-0000(70)80006-X'}])
add('6091',2018,'by','The specific exponential depth-three lower bound with an E-uniform explicit function is documented in the 2018 source. General constant-depth circuit lower bounds go back to the 1980s; that broader history does not fix the first date of this exact version.',('primary',))
add('6714',1985,'circa','Estimated origin in the 1980s study of highly parallel matching and circuit depth. This is the sharper nonuniform logarithmic-depth question; the broader NC matching problem and its later algorithms are not identical formulations.',('primary','quasinc'))
add('7268',1993,'year','Bellare, Goldwasser, Lund and Russell proposed the sliding-scale PCP conjecture in 1993. The card selects its polynomial-error, constant-query regime.',('primary',),sources=[{'title':'Efficient probabilistically checkable proofs and applications to approximations (STOC 1993)','url':'https://doi.org/10.1145/167088.167174'},{'title':'On the Sliding Scale Conjecture (2014)','url':'https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2014/030/download/','locator':'Introduction, attribution to 1993'}])
add('7363',1988,'circa','Estimated origin for the NP-membership question around the 1980s complexity results for existential real feasibility, including Canny’s 1988 PSPACE upper bound. The name of the modern complexity class is newer, and real-algebraic decision procedures are much older.',('er',))
add('6006',2016,'year','Dohrau, Gärtner, Kohler, Matoušek and Welzl introduced ARRIVAL in a 2016 preprint; the later publication and two-destination presentation do not make it a new problem.',('primary',),sources=[{'title':'ARRIVAL: A zero-player graph game in NP ∩ coNP (2016)','url':'https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.03546'}])
